            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Oct 8</td><td class="px-4 py-3">99 (86)</td><td class="px-4 py-3">76 (82)</td><td class="px-4 py-3">86 (&lt;5)</td><td class="px-4 py-3">94 (115)</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        Two additions round out the Care picture. On August 6, 2026 the program ran its only Care: Education draw so far (French-speaking teachers, minimum 68, fewer than five invitations). And the one-time <strong>Temporary Rural/Remote Health Support Initiative</strong>, for health-authority employees in cleaning and security jobs outside the excluded regional districts, had two draws: July 23 (minimum 50, 60 invitations) and September 17 (minimum 60, 33 invitations). That initiative is capped at up to 250 nominations and its registration window closed on October 7, 2026.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">What the Care and Build numbers show</h3>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
        <li><strong>Health fell fastest.</strong> The Care: Health cutoff dropped 32 points in four months, from 108 in May to 76 in September, and held at 76 in October. That is consistent with a fairly small pool of registrants in the 31 priority health occupations who also meet the program's conditions.</li>
        <li><strong>Childcare eased slowly.</strong> ECE cutoffs slid from 115 to 99. The two biggest ECE rounds (183 and 182 invitations in August and September) came after the August 18 allocation increase.</li>
        <li><strong>Construction bounced.</strong> Trades fell from 108 to 88 by August, then rose to 94 in September and October. A rising cutoff usually means the program reached deeper into the pool and is now waiting for new registrations to accumulate. Note that the May 6 Build draw explicitly included workers with apprenticeships registered with SkilledTradesBC, not only certified journeypersons.</li>
        <li><strong>Veterinary is tiny and volatile.</strong> With fewer than 10 invitations per round, a single high or low scorer moves the cutoff, which is why it swung from 72 to 90.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">Innovate: High Economic Impact draws</h2>

      <p>
        Innovate draws have no occupation list. They kept the same two-track design as the February to April rounds, and both thresholds drifted down through the year.
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-8">
