      <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">Who should act differently because of this recap</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
        <li><strong>Priority-occupation workers without the credential:</strong> start the certification now (ECE Registry, SkilledTradesBC, Care Aide Registry or your licensing body). That paperwork is what decides whether you are in a 76-point contest or a 131-point one.</li>
        <li><strong>Non-priority workers scoring under 120:</strong> 2026 offered no realistic BC PNP points route for you. Look at wage growth, a regional job offer, a higher language score, or other options in our <a href="/articles/bc-pnp-express-entry-bc-eebc-guide-2026" class="text-blue-600 underline">Express Entry BC guide</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>High earners:</strong> the 2026 wage track went as low as $52/hr and $105,000/yr. Keep your registration current and accurate. Note that a wage raised only to hit a threshold can lead to refusal under the program guide.</li>
      </ul>

